        </h2>
        
        <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <div class="space-y-8">
            <div class="text-left">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">
                Can you fix a window lock without replacing the whole window?
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-neutral-700">
                Often, yes. Many issues are resolved by replacing the handle, the gearbox/mechanism, or the keep, plus correcting alignment so the lock engages properly.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-left">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">
                What if I've lost my window keys?
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-neutral-700">
                In many cases, the solution is a lockable handle replacement or a compatible locking component change. The right option depends on your window type and how it currently locks.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-left">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">
                My handle turns but the window won't lock — what does that mean?
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-neutral-700">
                This commonly points to a stripped spindle, a failed gearbox, or misalignment where the locking points aren't meeting the keeps.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-left">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">
                Can you match my existing handle style or colour?
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-neutral-700">
                Usually, yes — within the limits of what's available for your handle type. For older setups, the priority is correct fit and secure operation, then appearance.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-left">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">
                Do you handle sash windows, tilt-and-turn, or timber windows?
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-neutral-700">
                These can be covered, but hardware varies more than standard uPVC casements. The key is identifying the lock type and fitting the correct components for that specific window.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="text-left">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">
                Why does my window lock feel stiff in cold weather?
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-lg text-neutral-700">
                Temperature changes can affect alignment and friction. If stiffness is persistent, it's worth addressing alignment and checking for wear rather than forcing the handle.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
